WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.500
A strawberry plant sends a thin stem along the ground.

2
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.600
Where it touches soil, it can grow roots.

3
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:15.700
It becomes a new plant with the same genetic information as its parent.

4
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:21.360
Brothers and sisters have the same two parents, and they usually look different.

5
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:26.500
Why don't you look exactly like your parents, or like your brothers and sisters?

6
00:00:27.433 --> 00:00:30.233
A runner is asexual reproduction.

7
00:00:31.113 --> 00:00:32.193
It has one parent.

8
00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:37.733
The offspring, the new living things, are genetically the same as the parent.

9
00:00:39.053 --> 00:00:40.813
Sexual reproduction is different.

10
00:00:41.753 --> 00:00:45.733
Two sex cells join, usually one from each of two parents.

11
00:00:46.633 --> 00:00:49.813
The offspring resemble their parents, but they are not copies.

12
00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:55.807
In a body cell, such as a skin cell, chromosomes come in pairs.

13
00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:59.667
A chromosome pair is two matching chromosomes.

14
00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:03.107
One comes from your mother, and one from your father.

15
00:01:04.107 --> 00:01:09.307
A typical human body cell has 46 chromosomes, in 23 pairs.

16
00:01:10.467 --> 00:01:14.287
Before the cell makes sex cells, each chromosome is copied.

17
00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:17.807
A copied chromosome is still one chromosome.

18
00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:22.620
Meiosis is the cell division that makes sex cells.

19
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:26.780
Each sex cell gets one chromosome from each pair.

20
00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:29.660
So it has half of the parent's chromosomes.

21
00:01:30.620 --> 00:01:34.720
A human egg or sperm normally has 23 chromosomes.

22
00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:40.410
Each pair splits up on its own, without regard to the other pairs.

23
00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:44.430
So each sex cell gets a mix chosen by chance.

24
00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:48.230
An allele is one version of a gene.

25
00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:52.250
Say a parent has alleles B and b.

26
00:01:53.090 --> 00:01:58.990
Each sex cell has a 50% chance of carrying B. It has the same chance of carrying b.

28
00:02:00.333 --> 00:02:05.093
Fertilization joins a sperm and an egg into one new cell.

29
00:02:06.013 --> 00:02:10.533
In humans, 23 chromosomes plus 23 make 46.

30
00:02:11.733 --> 00:02:15.913
The fertilized egg has full pairs again, one from each parent.

31
00:02:16.913 --> 00:02:19.693
Each child grows from a different egg and sperm.

32
00:02:20.753 --> 00:02:25.173
Each sex cell is a different mix, so brothers and sisters usually differ.

33
00:02:25.173 --> 00:02:29.533
A runner has one parent, so it is genetically the same.
